<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?><transcript><text start="1.72" dur="6.28">So, I&amp;#39;m going to South Carolina.</text><text start="5" dur="6.36">We&amp;#39;re going to hopefully get Darleen</text><text start="8" dur="5.72">Graham elected. She&amp;#39;s fantastic.</text><text start="11.36" dur="4.04">Sister Lindsey, and</text><text start="13.72" dur="3.28">we have a tremendous crowd as we have</text><text start="15.4" dur="3.6">always had.</text><text start="17" dur="4.48">And I think it&amp;#39;ll be an amazing day. We</text><text start="19" dur="5.68">had a very good meeting just now.</text><text start="21.48" dur="5.04">As you know, on cyber cyber security.</text><text start="24.68" dur="3.96">And that&amp;#39;s in full play, and we&amp;#39;re going</text><text start="26.52" dur="4.08">to do very well. Should have been done</text><text start="28.64" dur="4.4">many years ago by</text><text start="30.6" dur="3.88">other administrations.</text><text start="33.04" dur="3.92">And you have any quick questions? Go</text><text start="34.48" dur="2.48">ahead.</text><text start="42.48" dur="2.88">Where is this? Where?</text><text start="51.6" dur="3.72">I don&amp;#39;t know anything about it. I heard</text><text start="53.28" dur="3.88">that there&amp;#39;s something where his her</text><text start="55.32" dur="3.52">mother went against her.</text><text start="57.16" dur="4">I don&amp;#39;t know what that has to do with</text><text start="58.84" dur="4.32">the thing.</text><text start="61.16" dur="3.359">I just don&amp;#39;t know that. And</text><text start="63.16" dur="3">as you know,</text><text start="64.519" dur="3.481">well, I guess you know, if it was about</text><text start="66.16" dur="3.96">a Republican, I can guarantee you they&amp;#39;d</text><text start="68" dur="4.56">let it go. So, that&amp;#39;s why you&amp;#39;re asking.</text><text start="70.12" dur="5.8">The fact is I know nothing about it.</text><text start="72.56" dur="4.88">But, I hear the mother went very rogue</text><text start="75.92" dur="3.24">on the daughter, doesn&amp;#39;t have a lot of</text><text start="77.44" dur="3.72">respect for the daughter.</text><text start="79.16" dur="4.44">And I think the mother is a witness to</text><text start="81.16" dur="4.72">things also. So, who knows? And you&amp;#39;ll</text><text start="83.6" dur="5.04">have to figure that out. It&amp;#39;s a very</text><text start="85.88" dur="4.72">unusual situation to have a mother hate</text><text start="88.64" dur="5.92">a daughter that much. But, I don&amp;#39;t think</text><text start="90.6" dur="3.96">that has anything to do with the thing.</text><text start="103.92" dur="3.68">I don&amp;#39;t know that they are. I mean,</text><text start="105.84" dur="4.32">you&amp;#39;re telling me something. I wouldn&amp;#39;t</text><text start="107.6" dur="2.56">know that.</text><text start="117.96" dur="1.84">Well, I&amp;#39;ll tell you the interesting</text><text start="119.52" dur="2.68">thing</text><text start="119.8" dur="4.4">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; is you know we have a gentleman coming</text><text start="122.2" dur="3.6">home from Russia that they&amp;#39;ve been after</text><text start="124.2" dur="3.839">for years. He was</text><text start="125.8" dur="4.08">uh captured or taken during the Biden</text><text start="128.039" dur="3.801">administration. Uh wouldn&amp;#39;t have</text><text start="129.88" dur="3.2">happened if I were president, but he he</text><text start="131.84" dur="3.96">was taken</text><text start="133.08" dur="3.56">and he&amp;#39;s a highly respected man, Mr. Hu</text><text start="135.8" dur="2.24">bbard.</text><text start="136.64" dur="4.319">Stephen Hubbard.</text><text start="138.04" dur="4.8">And we were in the midst of negotiating</text><text start="140.959" dur="4.641">and a lot of stupid people said and</text><text start="142.84" dur="4.2">people that don&amp;#39;t know how life works,</text><text start="145.6" dur="3.68">they said, &amp;quot;Why aren&amp;#39;t you putting</text><text start="147.04" dur="4.28">righteous sanctions or all this in the</text><text start="149.28" dur="6">midst of a negotiation to try and get a</text><text start="151.32" dur="5.44">long-term hostage back from uh Russia?&amp;quot;</text><text start="155.28" dur="3">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Russia anything in exchange?</text><text start="156.76" dur="4.16">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; If I would have done that, you would not</text><text start="158.28" dur="4.24">have Mr. Hubbard coming back. Right now,</text><text start="160.92" dur="3.72">right now and you don&amp;#39;t know anything. I</text><text start="162.52" dur="4.76">mean, you&amp;#39;re fake news CNN. Look, right</text><text start="164.64" dur="5.12">now you have a man that&amp;#39;s beautifully</text><text start="167.28" dur="4.92">flying from Russia to wherever he&amp;#39;s</text><text start="169.76" dur="4.96">landing in the United States that I got</text><text start="172.2" dur="5.72">out because I had a very good and very</text><text start="174.72" dur="5.08">fast negotiation with President Putin.</text><text start="177.92" dur="3.8">If you would have put those sanctions on</text><text start="179.8" dur="3.4">or whatever you want to call them, uh</text><text start="181.72" dur="3.16">you could forget about him. You&amp;#39;d never</text><text start="183.2" dur="3.88">see him again. He&amp;#39;d be back in jail for</text><text start="184.88" dur="4.52">25 years. The other thing, very</text><text start="187.08" dur="4.48">important, when negotiating with Russia</text><text start="189.4" dur="4.839">right now on Ukraine,</text><text start="191.56" dur="5">uh we are maybe close to a deal for the</text><text start="194.239" dur="4.28">first time in a long time. We&amp;#39;re maybe</text><text start="196.56" dur="3.399">close to a deal. When you&amp;#39;re close to a</text><text start="198.519" dur="4.081">deal and you have very delicate</text><text start="199.959" dur="5.841">negotiations, you don&amp;#39;t put sanctions</text><text start="202.6" dur="6.12">on. And the other thing, we have uh</text><text start="205.8" dur="5.64">decimated Iran. Russia has had very</text><text start="208.72" dur="4.4">little input into Iran. They have</text><text start="211.44" dur="3.48">Certainly, they could have done a lot</text><text start="213.12" dur="4">more, but I&amp;#39;m not sure they did almost</text><text start="214.92" dur="4.2">anything. Uh that&amp;#39;s something that you</text><text start="217.12" dur="5">have to take into consideration also.</text><text start="219.12" dur="6">So, we beat Iran. We continue to beat</text><text start="222.12" dur="5.68">Iran and Russia and China, frankly, have</text><text start="225.12" dur="4.839">not been certainly much of a player and</text><text start="227.8" dur="4.439">we appreciate that. So, the people that</text><text start="229.959" dur="3.721">say that, &amp;quot;Oh, let&amp;#39;s put sanctions on.&amp;quot;</text><text start="232.239" dur="4.921">You know, I have the right to do them at</text><text start="233.68" dur="5.24">any day. If If they behave badly, if</text><text start="237.16" dur="2.72">they be</text><text start="238.92" dur="2.72">You don&amp;#39;t know what you&amp;#39;re talking</text><text start="239.88" dur="3.4">about. You&amp;#39;re a dummy. You&amp;#39;re a low IQ</text><text start="241.64" dur="4.36">person. You&amp;#39;re a dummy and you work for</text><text start="243.28" dur="5.36">CNN. Let me tell you, if I&amp;#39;m negotiating</text><text start="246" dur="5.48">to get a man back, a man that we wanted</text><text start="248.64" dur="6.08">back for years, a man that was a</text><text start="251.48" dur="4.599">prisoner in Siberia or some place in</text><text start="254.72" dur="3.359">Russia, and we&amp;#39;re getting him back</text><text start="256.079" dur="3.681">because of me. Should have been brought</text><text start="258.079" dur="2.961">It should have never happened, but it</text><text start="259.76" dur="2.96">should have been brought back during</text><text start="261.04" dur="4.8">Biden cuz he was there with during the</text><text start="262.72" dur="5.32">Biden. It was He was captured or taken</text><text start="265.84" dur="4.6">during Biden. When you&amp;#39;re negotiating</text><text start="268.04" dur="4.92">that and you&amp;#39;re dropping and I know that</text><text start="270.44" dur="4.68">I&amp;#39;m doing it and because a lot of people</text><text start="272.96" dur="4.88">didn&amp;#39;t know and they say, &amp;quot;Oh, let&amp;#39;s put</text><text start="275.12" dur="4.799">sanctions on Russia.&amp;quot; The negotiation</text><text start="277.84" dur="5.84">would obviously come immediately to an</text><text start="279.919" dur="3.761">end. So, use your head.</text><text start="290.72" dur="3.16">I don&amp;#39;t I don&amp;#39;t know.</text><text start="292.36" dur="2.4">No, I think it&amp;#39;s one of the greatest</text><text start="293.88" dur="3.16">things</text><text start="294.76" dur="3.64">I think it&amp;#39;s one of the greatest I think</text><text start="297.04" dur="3.48">it&amp;#39;s one of the greatest things we&amp;#39;ve</text><text start="298.4" dur="4.56">done. We&amp;#39;ve stopped Iran from having a</text><text start="300.52" dur="4.04">nuclear weapon. It&amp;#39;s one of the best</text><text start="302.96" dur="3.56">things that we&amp;#39;ve done.</text><text start="304.56" dur="3.76">Uh it took a lot of courage to do it</text><text start="306.52" dur="4.32">because no other president was willing</text><text start="308.32" dur="4.96">to do it. And if we didn&amp;#39;t do it, Iran</text><text start="310.84" dur="6.28">would right now have already used</text><text start="313.28" dur="3.84">massive nuclear weapons.</text><text start="325" dur="3.44">No, I wasn&amp;#39;t involved. I wasn&amp;#39;t</text><text start="328.96" dur="4.12">I don&amp;#39;t know who did it, but I was not</text><text start="330.64" dur="2.44">involved.</text><text start="340.72" dur="2.84">Are you a stupid person? Who do you work</text><text start="342.56" dur="2.72">for?</text><text start="343.56" dur="5.4">You&amp;#39;re a stupid person. And by the way,</text><text start="345.28" dur="3.68">your network is the worst of all.</text><text start="355.96" dur="3.16">Yeah, we would have a meeting. We would</text><text start="357.48" dur="4.56">certainly have that as a meeting. Yeah.</text><text start="359.12" dur="2.92">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; How confident are you</text><text start="362.24" dur="4.8">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I can&amp;#39;t say I can&amp;#39;t say that it&amp;#39;s going</text><text start="365" dur="5.84">to happen, but having a meeting on</text><text start="367.04" dur="3.8">denuclearization is a very good thing.</text><text start="382.56" dur="2.68">I haven&amp;#39;t heard it.</text><text start="389.68" dur="4.68">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Recently your Treasury Department</text><text start="392.36" dur="4.8">announced sanctions against the cartels</text><text start="394.36" dur="5.12">in the West exposing the Mexican cartels</text><text start="397.16" dur="2.96">of their abuse of the American quarter</text><text start="399.48" dur="1.12">horses.</text><text start="400.12" dur="2.12">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Go ahead.</text><text start="400.6" dur="3.68">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; So, are you going to launch a full</text><text start="402.24" dur="2.92">investigation on these cartels?</text><text start="404.28" dur="2.52">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; do.</text><text start="405.16" dur="3.8">And I always have. Thank you.</text><text start="406.8" dur="2.16">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Thank you.</text></transcript>